# Rules for cameraserver touching vendor device types.
#
# This one keeps getting lost: it is in git HEAD, was deleted from the working
# tree at some point, and while it is gone the camera service is denied on MTK's
# *secure* dma-buf heaps - the ones the SVP/protected camera path allocates from
# (mtk_svp_region-aligned, mtk_prot_region-aligned, mtk_wfd_region-aligned,
# mtk_2d_fr_region, all on /dev/dma_heap).  The camera still takes normal photos
# and video without it, so it only shows up when a session runs.
#
# cameraserver and dmabuf_system_secure_heap_device are both plat-public, so the
# rule is fine here; there is no neverallow on the type (surfaceflinger,
# mediaserver, hal_graphics_allocator, mediaswcodec, system_server and every app
# already have it).
allow cameraserver dmabuf_system_secure_heap_device:chr_file r_file_perms;
